<title>FRANCE: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>FRANCE GOVERNMENT LIST (970612)</p>
<p> President (Inaugurated 17 May 95)..............Jacques CHIRAC</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>SOCIALIST-LED GOVERNMENT (Formed 4 June 97)</p>
<p>(See end of list for party affiliations)</p>
<p> Prime Minister (Took office 3 June 97)......Lionel JOSPIN (PS)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>Agriculture &amp; Fisheries....Louis LE PENSEC (PS)</p>
<p>Civil Service, Administrative</p>
<p>    Reform &amp; Decentralisation...........Emile ZUCCHARELLI (PRS)</p>
<p>Culture, Communication &amp; Government</p>
<p>    Spokeswoman.........Catherine TRAUTMANN (PS)</p>
<p> Defence.......Alain RICHARD (PS)</p>
<p> Economy, Finance &amp; Industry........Dominique STRAUSS-KAHN (PS)</p>
<p> Employment &amp; Solidarity......Martine AUBRY (PS)</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs.............Hubert VEDRINE (PS)</p>
<p>Infrastructure, Transport &amp; Housing..Jean-Claude GAYSSOT (PCF)</p>
<p> Interior..........Jean-Pierre CHEVENEMENT (MDC)</p>
<p>Justice....Elisabeth GUIGOU (PS)</p>
<p>National Education, Research &amp; Technology..Claude ALLEGRE (PS)</p>
<p>Regional Development &amp; Environment...Dominique VOYNET (Greens)</p>
<p>Relations with Parliament..Daniel VAILLANT (PS)</p>
<p> Youth &amp; Sports........Marie George BUFFET (PCF)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS DELEGATE:</p>
<p>Delegated to the foreign minister:</p>
<p>    European Affairs.......Pierre MOSCOVICI (PS)</p>
<p>Delegated to the national education, research &amp;</p>
<p>technology minister:</p>
<p>Schools...Segolene ROYAL (PS)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>SECRETARIES OF STATE:</p>
<p>At the Interior Ministry:</p>
<p>	Overseas Territories.............Jean-Jack QUEYRANNE (PS)</p>
<p>At the Employment &amp; Solidarity Ministry:</p>
<p>	Health..............Bernard KOUCHNER (PRS)</p>
<p>At the Foreign Ministry:</p>
<p>	Cooperation..........Charles JOSSELIN (PS)</p>
<p>At the Infrastructure, Transport &amp; Housing Ministry:</p>
<p>Housing...Louis BESSON (PS)</p>
<p>At the Economy, Finance &amp; Industry Ministry:</p>
<p>	Foreign Trade........Jacques DONDOUX (PRS)</p>
<p>	Budget..............Christian SAUTTER (PS)</p>
<p>Small, Medium Business, Commerce</p>
<p>	     &amp; Crafts......Marylise LEBRANCHU (PS)</p>
<p>	Industry............Christian PIERRET (PS)</p>
<p>At the Defence Ministry:</p>
<p>Veterans Affairs.Jean-Pierre MASSERET (PS)</p>
<p>At the Infrastructure, Transport &amp; Housing Ministry:</p>
<p>	Tourism...........Michelle DEMESSINE (PCF)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>PS -- Socialist Party</p>
<p>PCF -- French Communist Party</p>
<p>PRS -- Radical-Socialist Party</p>
<p>MDC -- Citizens Movement</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> National Assembly Speaker.......Laurent FABIUS</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor......Jean-Claude TRICHET</p>
